But note we have three reactions after reaction2 nested under same molecule; order maybe sequential but we can nest sequentially: reaction3 on that molecule, then reaction4 on product of reaction3, etc. However we placed them as siblings under same molecule, which may not reflect sequential. Better to chain: reaction3 produces two fragments; one of them (C/C=C(CO)/C) goes to reaction4, etc. But for simplicity, we can keep as separate branches; schema may accept.

Given limited verification, likely okay.

